    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag: it is `true` when the owner's city already holds between 40 and 49 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50). Since the existing `>= 50` rejection fires earlier in `addOwner`, by the time the flag is computed the same-city count is always `< 50`, so a plain `>= 40` check captures the 40\u201349 window exactly. The hard rejection is untouched.\n\nChanges, kept small and cohesive to minimize structural impact:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` boolean property to the Owner schema (drives DTO generation), mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning`.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `capacityWarning` field with a simple getter/setter (each CC 1), mirroring `possibleDuplicate`. Persistence is required because the test reads the value back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, which re-maps from the entity.\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one statement setting `owner.setCapacityWarning(...)` before save, reusing the same-city stream idiom already in the method (adds no new branch, so no CC growth).\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column (the hsqldb profile is the one tests run against, and the only maintained evolved schema).\n\nMapStruct auto-maps the same-named `capacityWarning` entity\u2192DTO, so no mapper change was needed. I avoided adding any helper methods or extra branches, which would have paid the large `WMC_other` of these classes again.",
